1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,422
In this lesson, we'll define the
derivative, the instantaneous rate of

2
00:00:04,422 --> 00:00:04,864
change.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,378
The slope of a secant line through x and x
plus h is f of x plus h minus f of x, over

4
00:00:13,378 --> 00:00:13,552
h.

5
00:00:14,002 --> 00:00:18,439
As h shrinks to zero, the secant line
turns into the tangent line.

6
00:00:19,567 --> 00:00:26,410
The derivative of f at a is the limit as h
approaches zero of f of a plus h minus f

7
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:27,481
of a, over h.

8
00:00:27,931 --> 00:00:31,686
It's the slope of the tangent line at a,
if that limit exists.

9
00:00:32,833 --> 00:00:39,023
For f of x equals x squared at a equals
three: three plus h squared minus nine,

10
00:00:39,023 --> 00:00:41,217
over h, which is six plus h.

11
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:44,953
The limit is six. So f prime of three
equals six.

12
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:50,772
We write f prime of a, or d y d x, or d d
x of f.

13
00:00:51,222 --> 00:00:53,654
They all mean the same thing: the
derivative.

14
00:00:54,800 --> 00:01:00,999
If s of t is position in meters and t is
in seconds, then s prime of t is velocity

15
00:01:00,999 --> 00:01:02,587
in meters per second.

16
00:01:03,037 --> 00:01:06,365
The derivative always has units of output
per input.

17
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:13,487
Your turn. Use the definition to find f
prime of one for f of x equals three x

18
00:01:13,487 --> 00:01:14,177
plus two.

19
00:01:14,627 --> 00:01:16,163
Pause the video and try it.

20
00:01:16,613 --> 00:01:22,799
Three times one plus h plus two minus
five, over h, is three. So f prime of one

21
00:01:22,799 --> 00:01:23,504
is three.

22
00:01:24,633 --> 00:01:29,774
In this lesson, we'll find the derivative
at every point at once, as a new function.

23
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:38,383
Replace a with x: f prime of x equals the
limit as h approaches zero of f of x plus

24
00:01:38,383 --> 00:01:40,457
h minus f of x, over h.

25
00:01:40,907 --> 00:01:42,635
This gives the slope at any x.

26
00:01:43,766 --> 00:01:50,488
For f of x equals x squared: x plus h
squared minus x squared, over h, is two x

27
00:01:50,488 --> 00:01:51,084
plus h.

28
00:01:51,534 --> 00:01:53,774
So f prime of x equals two x.

29
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:59,998
For f of x equals the square root of x,
multiply by the conjugate.

30
00:02:00,448 --> 00:02:07,638
x plus h minus x, over h times the square
root of x plus h plus the square root of

31
00:02:07,638 --> 00:02:10,795
x. The limit is one over two root x.

32
00:02:11,933 --> 00:02:18,219
We can sketch f prime from the graph of f:
where f rises, f prime is positive; where

33
00:02:18,219 --> 00:02:21,661
f falls, negative; at peaks and valleys,
zero.

34
00:02:22,111 --> 00:02:27,060
For a parabola opening up, f prime is a
line crossing zero at the vertex.

35
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:33,149
Going backward, if f prime is positive on
an interval, f is increasing there.

36
00:02:33,599 --> 00:02:36,500
And the steeper f is, the larger f prime
is.

37
00:02:36,633 --> 00:02:43,801
Your turn. Use the definition to find the
derivative of f of x equals x squared plus

38
00:02:43,801 --> 00:02:43,948
x.

39
00:02:44,398 --> 00:02:45,934
Pause the video and try it.

40
00:02:46,384 --> 00:02:51,440
Two x plus h plus one, so f prime of x
equals two x plus one.

41
00:02:52,566 --> 00:02:56,726
In this lesson, we'll see where a function
fails to have a derivative.

42
00:02:57,866 --> 00:03:03,443
f is differentiable at a if f prime of a
exists, meaning the graph has a single,

43
00:03:03,443 --> 00:03:05,674
non-vertical tangent line there.

44
00:03:06,124 --> 00:03:08,556
Smooth curves are differentiable
everywhere.

45
00:03:09,699 --> 00:03:15,151
At a corner, the left and right slopes
differ. The absolute value of x at zero

46
00:03:15,151 --> 00:03:19,065
has slope negative one on the left and one
on the right.

47
00:03:19,515 --> 00:03:21,605
So it isn't differentiable at zero.

48
00:03:22,733 --> 00:03:28,240
A cusp is a very sharp point, like x to
the two thirds at zero. A vertical

49
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:32,781
tangent, like the cube root of x at zero,
has infinite slope.

50
00:03:33,231 --> 00:03:35,001
Neither has a derivative there.

51
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:39,951
If f isn't continuous at a, it can't be
differentiable at a.

52
00:03:40,401 --> 00:03:43,132
A hole or a jump rules out a tangent line.

53
00:03:44,266 --> 00:03:48,767
Differentiability implies continuity, but
not the other way around.

54
00:03:49,217 --> 00:03:54,785
The absolute value function is continuous
at zero but not differentiable there.

55
00:03:55,933 --> 00:04:02,004
Your turn. Is f of x equals the absolute
value of x minus two differentiable at

56
00:04:02,004 --> 00:04:02,311
two?

57
00:04:02,761 --> 00:04:04,297
Pause the video and try it.

58
00:04:04,747 --> 00:04:07,115
No. It has a corner at x equals two.

59
00:04:08,233 --> 00:04:12,756
In this lesson, we'll learn the power
rule, the fastest shortcut in calculus.

60
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:19,020
The derivative of a constant is zero. A
horizontal line has slope zero.

61
00:04:19,470 --> 00:04:21,326
And the derivative of x is one.

62
00:04:22,466 --> 00:04:27,501
The power rule: the derivative of x to the
n is n x to the n minus one.

63
00:04:27,951 --> 00:04:31,471
The derivative of x to the fifth is five x
to the fourth.

64
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,562
It works for negative exponents.

65
00:04:35,012 --> 00:04:40,974
The derivative of x to the negative two is
negative two x to the negative three, or

66
00:04:40,974 --> 00:04:42,842
negative two over x cubed.

67
00:04:43,966 --> 00:04:45,716
And for fractional exponents.

68
00:04:46,166 --> 00:04:51,952
The derivative of x to the one half is one
half x to the negative one half, one over

69
00:04:51,952 --> 00:04:55,190
two root x, matching what we found with
limits.

70
00:04:56,333 --> 00:04:58,936
Rewrite roots and fractions as powers
first.

71
00:04:59,386 --> 00:05:05,148
One over the cube root of x is x to the
negative one third. Its derivative is

72
00:05:05,148 --> 00:05:08,815
negative one third x to the negative four
thirds.

73
00:05:09,933 --> 00:05:13,474
Your turn. Find the derivative of x to the
seven halves.

74
00:05:13,924 --> 00:05:15,460
Pause the video and try it.

75
00:05:15,910 --> 00:05:17,980
Seven halves x to the five halves.

76
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:23,606
In this lesson, we'll combine the power
rule with two simple rules to

77
00:05:23,606 --> 00:05:25,500
differentiate any polynomial.

78
00:05:26,633 --> 00:05:30,047
The derivative of c times f is c times f
prime.

79
00:05:30,497 --> 00:05:34,358
The derivative of seven x cubed is twenty
one x squared.

80
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:41,345
The derivative of f plus g is f prime plus
g prime, and the same for differences.

81
00:05:41,795 --> 00:05:43,566
Differentiate term by term.

82
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:50,996
Differentiate f of x equals four x to the
fifth minus three x squared plus six x

83
00:05:50,996 --> 00:05:51,783
minus two.

84
00:05:52,233 --> 00:05:55,326
Twenty x to the fourth minus six x plus
six.

85
00:05:56,467 --> 00:06:02,227
Find the tangent line to y equals x cubed
minus two x at x equals two.

86
00:06:02,677 --> 00:06:09,252
y prime is three x squared minus two,
which is ten at x equals two. The point is

87
00:06:09,252 --> 00:06:13,855
two, four. So y minus four equals ten
times x minus two.

88
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:19,800
Where does y equals x cubed minus three x
have horizontal tangents?

89
00:06:20,250 --> 00:06:26,245
Set three x squared minus three equal to
zero: x equals one or negative one.

90
00:06:27,367 --> 00:06:31,975
Your turn. Differentiate y equals two over
x plus five root x.

91
00:06:32,425 --> 00:06:33,961
Pause the video and try it.

92
00:06:34,411 --> 00:06:40,627
Rewrite as two x to the negative one plus
five x to the one half. The derivative is

93
00:06:40,627 --> 00:06:44,672
negative two over x squared plus five over
two root x.

94
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:50,247
In this lesson, we'll learn the
derivatives of four of the most important

95
00:06:50,247 --> 00:06:50,856
functions.

96
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,624
The derivative of sine x is cosine x.

97
00:06:55,074 --> 00:06:59,746
Look at the graphs: where sine is
steepest, at zero, cosine is at its peak.

98
00:07:00,867 --> 00:07:04,280
The derivative of cosine x is negative
sine x.

99
00:07:04,730 --> 00:07:09,935
Cosine starts at its top, slope zero, then
falls, matching negative sine.

100
00:07:11,067 --> 00:07:14,459
The derivative of e to the x is e to the x
itself.

101
00:07:14,909 --> 00:07:18,855
That's what makes e special: the slope
equals the height everywhere.

102
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:24,715
The derivative of ln x is one over x, for
x greater than zero.

103
00:07:25,165 --> 00:07:27,511
The log grows, but more and more slowly.

104
00:07:28,633 --> 00:07:34,649
Differentiate y equals three sine x minus
two e to the x plus four ln x.

105
00:07:35,099 --> 00:07:39,302
Three cosine x minus two e to the x plus
four over x.

106
00:07:40,433 --> 00:07:46,833
Your turn. Find the slope of y equals
cosine x plus x at x equals pi over two.

107
00:07:47,283 --> 00:07:48,819
Pause the video and try it.

108
00:07:49,269 --> 00:07:54,368
y prime is negative sine x plus one, which
is zero at pi over two.

109
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:58,828
In this lesson, we'll differentiate
products of functions.

110
00:07:59,967 --> 00:08:04,127
The derivative of a product is not the
product of the derivatives.

111
00:08:04,577 --> 00:08:09,654
x times x is x squared, with derivative
two x, not one times one.

112
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:16,155
The product rule: the derivative of f g is
f prime g plus f g prime.

113
00:08:16,605 --> 00:08:21,784
Derivative of the first times the second,
plus the first times the derivative of the

114
00:08:21,784 --> 00:08:22,215
second.

115
00:08:23,333 --> 00:08:25,467
Differentiate x squared sine x.

116
00:08:25,917 --> 00:08:29,053
Two x sine x plus x squared cosine x.

117
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:35,747
For x e to the x ln x, apply the rule
twice, or use the three-term version.

118
00:08:36,197 --> 00:08:43,559
Each term differentiates one factor: e to
the x ln x plus x e to the x ln x plus e

119
00:08:43,559 --> 00:08:44,367
to the x.

120
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:50,151
Find the slope of y equals x e to the x at
x equals zero.

121
00:08:50,601 --> 00:08:55,038
y prime is e to the x plus x e to the x,
which is one at zero.

122
00:08:56,167 --> 00:08:59,303
Your turn. Differentiate x cubed cosine x.

123
00:08:59,753 --> 00:09:01,289
Pause the video and try it.

124
00:09:01,739 --> 00:09:05,365
Three x squared cosine x minus x cubed
sine x.

125
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:06,500
Next time, we'll learn the quotient rule.
If this helped, subscribe to School Math,

126
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:09,103
In this lesson, we'll differentiate
quotients.

127
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:17,535
The derivative of f over g is g f prime
minus f g prime, all over g squared.

128
00:09:17,985 --> 00:09:22,187
Some remember low d high minus high d low,
over low squared.

129
00:09:23,333 --> 00:09:27,003
Differentiate x squared plus one, over x
minus three.

130
00:09:27,453 --> 00:09:34,108
x minus three times two x, minus x squared
plus one times one, over x minus three

131
00:09:34,108 --> 00:09:40,598
squared. That simplifies to x squared
minus six x minus one, over x minus three

132
00:09:40,598 --> 00:09:41,255
squared.

133
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:44,427
Differentiate sine x over x.

134
00:09:44,877 --> 00:09:48,247
x cosine x minus sine x, over x squared.

135
00:09:49,367 --> 00:09:55,961
Sometimes simplifying first is faster. x
cubed plus x over x is just x squared plus

136
00:09:55,961 --> 00:09:56,279
one.

137
00:09:56,729 --> 00:10:00,099
Its derivative is two x, no quotient rule
needed.

138
00:10:01,233 --> 00:10:07,129
A constant on top can be rewritten. Five
over x squared is five x to the negative

139
00:10:07,129 --> 00:10:07,420
two.

140
00:10:07,870 --> 00:10:10,878
The derivative is negative ten over x
cubed.

141
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,987
Your turn. Differentiate e to the x over
x.

142
00:10:15,437 --> 00:10:16,973
Pause the video and try it.

143
00:10:17,423 --> 00:10:24,164
x e to the x minus e to the x, over x
squared, or e to the x times x minus one,

144
00:10:24,164 --> 00:10:25,444
over x squared.

145
00:10:26,566 --> 00:10:31,079
In this lesson, we'll use the quotient
rule to find the derivatives of the

146
00:10:31,079 --> 00:10:32,603
remaining trig functions.

147
00:10:33,733 --> 00:10:39,225
Tangent is sine over cosine. By the
quotient rule: cosine squared plus sine

148
00:10:39,225 --> 00:10:41,349
squared, over cosine squared.

149
00:10:41,799 --> 00:10:47,252
That's one over cosine squared, so the
derivative of tangent x is secant squared

150
00:10:47,252 --> 00:10:47,388
x.

151
00:10:48,533 --> 00:10:53,823
Secant is one over cosine. Its derivative
is sine over cosine squared.

152
00:10:54,273 --> 00:10:56,044
That's secant x tangent x.

153
00:10:57,166 --> 00:11:02,969
Similarly, the derivative of cosecant x is
negative cosecant x cotangent x.

154
00:11:03,419 --> 00:11:07,920
And the derivative of cotangent x is
negative cosecant squared x.

155
00:11:09,066 --> 00:11:12,735
Notice the pattern: the co functions get a
negative sign.

156
00:11:13,185 --> 00:11:17,345
tan pairs with sec squared, cot with
negative csc squared.

157
00:11:18,466 --> 00:11:24,034
Find the tangent line to y equals tangent
x at x equals pi over four.

158
00:11:24,484 --> 00:11:30,848
The slope is secant squared of pi over
four, which is two. The point is pi over

159
00:11:30,848 --> 00:11:36,004
four, one. So y minus one equals two times
x minus pi over four.

160
00:11:37,133 --> 00:11:39,607
Your turn. Differentiate x secant x.

161
00:11:40,057 --> 00:11:41,593
Pause the video and try it.

162
00:11:42,043 --> 00:11:46,203
By the product rule: secant x plus x
secant x tangent x.

163
00:11:47,333 --> 00:11:52,829
Next time, we start Unit 3, the chain rule
and implicit differentiation. If this

164
00:11:52,829 --> 00:11:57,844
helped, subscribe to School Math,
Explained, and turn on notifications so

165
00:11:57,844 --> 00:12:00,111
you don't miss it. See you there.

